---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Home">
  <section class="band band-navy hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="bar"></span>
      <h1>Service should not start with debt.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We make sure those who choose to lead don't begin their service in debt.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/give" class="btn btn-give">Give</a>
        <a href="/how-it-works" class="btn btn-outline">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <h2>The math is broken.</h2>
        <div>
          <p class="lede">
            Becoming a military officer requires a college degree. The fully funded paths (service academies and full ROTC scholarships) reach only a fraction of the people who commission.
          </p>
          <p>
            Everyone else pays for some or all of their education themselves. They borrow, pick a cheaper school than the one that admitted them, or give up on service for a career that pays more.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once they commission, they can't earn their way out. Pay comes from a fixed public pay table, and deployments and moves make a second income nearly impossible. There is no side hustle in a deployment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="num">58%</span>
          <div class="label">Historically, roughly this share of new officers paid their own way through college (FY2000 data).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="num">$99,139</span>
          <div class="label">USC's cost of attendance for one year (2025–26). Many top universities that host ROTC units cost close to $100,000.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="num">16%</span>
          <div class="label">Share of four years at USC covered by the new $65,000 lifetime cap on federal parent loans, from July 1, 2026.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="num">137%</span>
          <div class="label">Rise in private tuition since Congress last set the ROTC cadet stipend ceiling, in FY2001.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin-top: 4.5rem;">
        <p>We don't lose these candidates in the interview. We lose them at the tuition bill.</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-navy">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Chosen to lead.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Our recipients have already committed: a high schooler signing up for ROTC, or an enlisted service member going after the degree to commission. We fill the middle, the gap between where scholarships and family help end and the bill begins.
      </p>
      <div class="tracks">
        <div class="track">
          <span class="bar"></span>
          <h3>High school candidates</h3>
          <p class="hook">“You chose to lead. We'll help you get there without the debt.”</p>
          <p>Juniors and seniors headed to a college with ROTC, or in service academy prep.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="track">
          <span class="bar"></span>
          <h3>Enlisted service members</h3>
          <p class="hook">“You already answered the call. Now lead.”</p>
          <p>Active-duty enlisted members of any branch pursuing the degree they need to commission, through programs such as Green to Gold, STA-21 or OCS/OTS.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="/how-it-works">Who's eligible and how we choose →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-steel">
    <div class="container split">
      <h2>Every dollar reaches the candidate.</h2>
      <div>
        <ul class="bars">
          <li>A volunteer board with minimal overhead</li>
          <li>Money paid directly to schools, never to individuals</li>
          <li>Enrollment and academic progress checked before every payment</li>
          <li>An independent selection committee with conflict-of-interest rules</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/give" class="btn btn-give">Give</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band-navy">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="bar"></span>
      <h2>Built by people who've lived it.</h2>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <p>“I got lucky. I would like to be somebody else's luck.”</p>
        <cite>Chris Kennedy, co-founder</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p style="margin-top: 2.5rem;"><a href="/our-story">Read our story →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
